menuconfig HCP_INPUT
	bool "HCP input (button, debounced GPIO interrupt)"
	default y
	depends on GPIO
	help
	  User button on the devicetree `sw0` alias. The pin interrupts on both edges
	  and the line is sampled once the contact has stopped bouncing, so an idle
	  device runs nothing for the button (it used to poll every 5 ms). No wakeup
	  source: this collector does not sleep.

if HCP_INPUT

config HCP_INPUT_DEBOUNCE_MS
	int "Debounce settle time (ms)"
	default 30
	help
	  Both the window an edge waits before the pin is sampled again and the time a
	  level must hold before it is reported as settled (Debouncer). 30 ms is well
	  below what a hand can produce and well above typical contact bounce.

endif
